From Culture Identifica tion to Na tiona l Identifica tion
—On Important Role of Traditional Chinese Culture in the Formation
and Development of the Hui Ethnic Group
L IW ei,D INGM ing2jun
(Beifang Ethnic University, Yinchuan 750021, China)
Abstract: The Hui ethnic group is an important member of Chinese big fam ily.
In history, Islam played an important
role in the formation of the Hui ethnic group. Meanwhile, the Hui ethnic group is a m inority formed in China.
In its forma2
tion and development, it absorbed and carried a lot of traditional Chinese culture, and it also underwent a high identifica2
tion process of traditional Chinese culture, Chinese nation and China.
Culture identification is an important strategic re2
source for maintaining national security and unity.
The value system of“promoting unity”of Chinese culture has been ac2
cepted by the Hui ethnic group and guides each member’s thinking and behavior.
Since modern times, the Hui ethnic
groups has made its due contribution to China in opposing separation, fighting against invading of the enemy, maintaining
national unity, safeguarding state sovereignty and territorial integrity. This is closely relation to the Hui ethnic group’s high
identification of traditional Chinese culture.
Key words: the Hui ethnic group; culture identification; national identification

